451. Design automation framework from scratch.
⭐ Interview Answer

“I would first understand the application, test types, environments, execution requirements and CI/CD setup. Then I would design the framework in a modular way so that UI, API, test data, reporting, logging and configuration are separated.

For a Selenium Java framework, I would typically use Java + Selenium + TestNG + Maven + Page Object Model, along with utilities for waits, screenshots, configuration and test data.

The structure would contain separate layers for test cases, page objects, utilities, configuration, test data, API/database utilities and reporting.

I would also integrate the framework with Git and Jenkins for CI/CD, support parallel execution using TestNG, and make browser/environment selection configurable rather than hard-coded.

Finally, I would add logging, screenshots on failure, reports, retry handling for controlled flaky failures, and proper test-data management.”

