463. How would you handle flaky tests?
⭐ Strong answer

“First I would identify the actual reason for flakiness rather than immediately adding retries.

Common causes include synchronization issues, unstable locators, test-data conflicts, environment instability and shared state.

I would use explicit waits, stable locators, independent test data and proper cleanup.

For genuinely transient failures, I could implement a limited retry mechanism, but I would also report retries separately so that retries don't hide product defects.”

🔥 Excellent line

“Retry should be a safety net, not a solution for bad automation.”

